// =============================================================================
//  triage-session.json — the ONE file shared by the three steps of the loop
// =============================================================================
//
//  Location:  D:\Gabriel\OneDrive\Claude\Workspace\Personal Assistance\email-triage\triage-session.json
//
//  Step 1  pa-email-triage        (Cowork skill)  → CREATES the file
//  Step 2  triage-review.html     (Gabriel)       → EDITS decisions; Confirm or Skip ONE GROUP at a time
//  Step 3  pa-email-triage-save   (Cowork skill)  → once no group is pending, APPLIES every "reviewed" group
//
//  This is an annotated example, not a formal JSON Schema. Every key is listed
//  with WHO writes it. The general rule for all three steps: load the whole
//  JSON, mutate only the keys you own, write the whole JSON back — never drop a
//  key you don't understand.
//
//  ─── Tasks live in Google Tasks / Microsoft To Do — there is NO Notion ──────
//  One backend per mailbox, no cross-posting and no list picking:
//     Gmail (Gabriel & Arina) → Google Tasks, default list   (provider "gtasks")
//     Outlook                 → Microsoft To Do, default list (provider "todo")
//  A task's IDENTITY is its `key` = "<provider>:<listId>:<taskId>". Emails point
//  at one with `existingTaskKey`. `url` is an optional display link and may be
//  null. There are no groups and no task tags anywhere in this file.
//
//  ─── Groups / tabs (exactly two — there is NO session-level status) ─────────
//  The file holds two independent review queues ("groups"). Each has its own
//  status; nothing else in the file carries a status. `groups` has exactly the
//  keys "gabriel" and "gabriel-arina" — never a third one.
//
//     group key       | tab label       | which emails          | which tasks
//     ----------------+-----------------+-----------------------+---------------------
//     "gabriel"       | Gabriel         | source !== "gmail"    | provider === "todo"
//     "gabriel-arina" | Gabriel & Arina | source === "gmail"    | provider === "gtasks"
//
//  Group status lifecycle (one per group):
//     "pending-review"        → written by step 1; the tab is editable on the page
//     "reviewed"              → step 2, Confirm & Save on that tab; tab locked
//     "skipped"               → step 2, Skip on that tab; tab locked (Reopen puts it back to pending)
//     "processed"             → step 3, after applying a "reviewed" group
//     "processed-with-errors" → step 3, same but at least one item failed
//  "skipped" groups stay "skipped" forever (step 3 never touches them).
//  Step 3 refuses to run while EITHER group is still "pending-review".
//
//  ─── Threads: one row per conversation ─────────────────────────────────────
//  For every thread with at least one message in the inbox, step 1 writes EVERY
//  message of that thread into emails[], each with:
//     threadId    Gmail threadId / Outlook conversationId
//     threadRole  "head" (exactly one per thread — the NEWEST message) | "child"
//     inInbox     false = already archived; it is NEVER moved back to the inbox
//  `category`, `suggestedTask`, `existingTaskKey` and `newInThread` are HEAD-ONLY
//  — there is never more than one task per thread. The page shows only the head
//  as an interactive row (children are collapsed, muted and read-only) and
//  DERIVES every child decision from the head's action:
//
//     head's action                              | child action                | child flagged
//     -------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+--------------
//     flag / create-task / update-task           | "flag" if inInbox, else     | false
//                                                | "archive"                   |
//     archive / complete-task / cancel-task      | "archive"                   | false
//
//  Only the head is ever starred. Counts and filters on the page are per thread.
//
//  ─── Fixed vocabularies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  provider : "gtasks" | "todo"
//  category : "Important" | "FYI" | "Not Important"        (heads only)
//  emailAction (non-tracked head — chosen from the category):
//             Not Important → "archive"                              (locked)
//             FYI           → "archive" (default) | "flag"
//             Important     → "create-task" (default) | "flag" | "archive"
//  emailAction (tracked head, i.e. existingTaskKey set — no category):
//                             "update-task" (default) | "complete-task" | "cancel-task"
//             …unless the matched task is already `status: "completed"`, in which
//             case "archive" is the ONLY action and nothing is written to the task.
//  emailAction (child): derived, never chosen — "flag" | "archive" (table above).
//
//  What each emailAction means for step 3 — the action decides INBOX vs ARCHIVE only:
//     "archive"        archive the email                                   (leaves inbox)
//     "flag"           keep the email in the inbox (page label: "Keep in inbox")
//     "create-task"    create decision.task ?? suggestedTask in the mailbox's task app; keep in inbox
//     "update-task"    apply existingTasks[].decision.edits of the matched task; keep in inbox
//     "complete-task"  complete the matched task      AND archive the thread
//     "cancel-task"    complete the matched task with a "Cancelled …" note line AND archive the thread
//  Every email therefore ends up either in the inbox or archived.
//  Never delete an email, never reply, never draft.
//
//  ─── Star / flag is its OWN property: decision.flagged ──────────────────────
//   • `isFlagged`        (step 1) = current state: Gmail has label STARRED / Outlook flagStatus "flagged"
//   • `decision.flagged` (step 2) = wanted state after the save, for EVERY email (both mailboxes)
//   • It is independent of the action: an archived email may stay starred, an
//     inbox email may be unstarred. Page default = isFlagged; choosing a
//     keep-in-inbox action ("flag" / "create-task" / "update-task") switches it ON
//     as a convenience, Gabriel can toggle it back. Children are always false —
//     only the head of a thread carries the star.
//   • Step 3: flagged !== isFlagged → Gmail add/remove STARRED, Outlook flag_email
//     "flagged" / "notFlagged"; equal → nothing. Applied for every action, after
//     the archive/keep step. Outcome "starred" | "unstarred" | "flagged" | "unflagged".
//
//  ─── Gmail labels are EMAIL-ONLY ────────────────────────────────────────────
//   • Step 1 records the USER-CREATED labels only (never system labels such as
//     INBOX, UNREAD, STARRED, IMPORTANT, SENT, DRAFT, SPAM, TRASH, CATEGORY_*):
//       - `gmailLabels`      = every user label that exists in the mailbox
//       - `emails[].labels`  = the user labels currently on that email
//   • Step 2 lets Gabriel toggle labels on the email (`decision.labels`); the page
//     offers gmailLabels ∪ whatever is already set. They mirror NOTHING on a task.
//   • Step 3 applies the diff to the message only: add = decision.labels − labels,
//     remove = labels − decision.labels (creating a missing Gmail label first).
//   • `systemLabels` (step 1, gmail): every OTHER label on the message — EXCEPT
//     INBOX and STARRED, which are modelled by the action and decision.flagged.
//     Read-only: shown muted on the page, never edited, never written back.
//   • Outlook emails have no labels: `labels` / `systemLabels` / `decision.labels` are absent.
//   • Their ONE task-side effect is the title PREFIX a new task is created with
//     (case-insensitive, creation only, never re-applied to an existing task):
//         properties/mount st    → "Mount: <title>"
//         properties/arura st    → "Arura: <title>"
//         properties/St Huberts  → "Huberts: <title>"
//
//  ─── Task descriptions: two sections, plain text ────────────────────────────
//     -- notes
//     <Gabriel's own text, typed in the task itself. Step 1 READS it and takes it
//      into account; nothing ever rewrites it. The page lets Gabriel edit exactly
//      this half.>
//
//     -- auto --
//     One line: what this is and what needs to be done.
//     26 Aug — one dated line per message of the thread, oldest first, newest 10
//     Latest email: <deep link to the NEWEST message of the thread>
//     [triage] thread=<threadId> src=gmail|outlook
//
//  Everything below `-- auto --` is regenerated by step 1 on every run; the page
//  shows it read-only. The `[triage]` footer is how the next run re-finds the task
//  (Google Tasks has no custom fields); on To Do it is mirrored into
//  linkedResources[0].externalId. Plain text, no markdown — Google Tasks has no
//  formatting. `decision.edits.notes` is always the WHOLE new description.
//
//  Other hard rules:
//   • A task TITLE is written once, at creation. It is never renamed afterwards —
//     Gabriel may have renamed it himself — so there is no `title` key in `edits`
//     and the page shows the title of an existing task read-only.
//   • existingTaskKey, when set, must equal the `key` of one existingTasks[] entry.
//   • An already-completed task is read-only end to end: no edits, no reopen.
// =============================================================================
{
  // ── Session-level ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Step 1. ISO-8601 timestamp of when the triage ran. The page shows its age.
  "generatedAt": "2026-08-31T08:00:00.000Z",

  // Step 1 (informational). Which mailboxes were actually fetched this run —
  // e.g. ["outlook"] when the Gmail connector was down. The page ignores it.
  "mailboxes": ["outlook", "gmail"],

  // Step 1. All USER-CREATED labels of the Gabriel & Arina Gmail (system labels excluded).
  // The page offers these as toggles on Gmail email rows.
  "gmailLabels": ["Travel", "properties/mount st", "properties/St Huberts"],

  // Per-group status — THE thing step 3 keys off. Exactly two keys. Step 1 must
  // write both as "pending-review". There is deliberately no top-level "status".
  "groups": {
    "gabriel": {
      "status": "pending-review",   // see lifecycle above
      "reviewedAt": null,           // step 2: ISO timestamp of Confirm or Skip on this tab (null again after Reopen)
      "processedAt": null           // step 3: ISO timestamp when this group was applied
    },
    "gabriel-arina": {
      "status": "pending-review",
      "reviewedAt": null,
      "processedAt": null
    }
  },

  // ── Emails ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Step 1 writes every field except `decision` (may be omitted; the page fills
  // it in) and `outcome` (step 3 only). REQUIRED from step 1 on every message:
  // id, source, sourceId, from, subject, date, summary, isFlagged, threadId,
  // threadRole, inInbox — plus, on heads only, category / existingTaskKey /
  // suggestedTask / newInThread. Every message of an inbox thread is listed.
  "emails": [
    {
      // ── A tracked GMAIL head (newest message of its thread) ──
      // Mailbox message id: the deep link on the page AND what step 3 acts on
      // (archive / star / labels), so it must be the real id for that source.
      "id": "18f3a2b9c0d1e999",
      "source": "gmail",            // "gmail" → gabriel-arina tab · "outlook" → gabriel tab
      "sourceId": "gmail:18f3a2b9c0d1e999",   // "<source>:<id>"
      "from": "Arina <arina@example.com>",
      "subject": "Re: Mount St plumber quote",
      "date": "2026-08-31T03:40:00.000Z",
      "summary": "Quote v2 arrived, $1,240, needs approval by Friday.",  // 1-2 lines; also feeds the auto block
      "isFlagged": true,            // step 1: current star (Gmail) / flag (Outlook) state
      "labels": ["properties/mount st"],   // step 1: USER labels on the email right now (editable)
      "systemLabels": ["IMPORTANT"],       // step 1: the rest, minus INBOX/STARRED (read-only)

      "threadId": "18f3a2b9c0d1e000",      // gmail threadId / outlook conversationId
      "threadRole": "head",                // exactly one head per thread — the newest message
      "inInbox": true,                     // false = already archived; never un-archive
      "newInThread": true,                 // head only: newer than the message the task points at (page badge)

      // Step 1's classification; Gabriel can change it on the page. Drives the
      // default emailAction. Absent on children; unused when tracked.
      "category": "Important",

      // null for a NEW topic. Set to the `key` of a matching task to mark the
      // thread as "tracked" — it then only offers update/complete/cancel.
      "existingTaskKey": "gtasks:MTIz:abc789",

      // Step 1's proposed task for Important heads (null when nothing to suggest,
      // and always null for tracked heads). Same shape as decision.task.
      "suggestedTask": null,

      // Step 2 (the page) owns this block. Step 1 may omit it entirely.
      "decision": {
        "emailAction": "update-task",   // vocabulary above; ALWAYS one of the allowed values for this email
        "isTask": false,                // derived: emailAction === "create-task". Never read it, read emailAction.
        "flagged": true,                // step 2: wanted star/flag state (see header). Step 3 diffs vs isFlagged.
        "labels": ["properties/mount st"],  // step 2, gmail only: wanted USER labels (step 3 diffs vs `labels`)
        // Gabriel's edited copy of the task to create. null means "use
        // suggestedTask unchanged", and it is always null unless the action is
        // "create-task" (for which the page guarantees one of the two exists).
        "task": null
      },

      // Step 3 only — the page never writes it and shows it read-only in the
      // processed summary. A short human string, e.g. "archived", "starred",
      // "task created", "task updated", "task already completed",
      // "labels +Travel −House", "FAILED: <reason>" (anything matching /fail/i
      // is shown red). Absent until processed.
      "outcome": "task updated"
    },
    {
      // ── A CHILD of that same thread: read-only on the page ──
      // No category, no suggestedTask, no existingTaskKey, no newInThread.
      "id": "18f3a2b9c0d1e000",
      "source": "gmail",
      "sourceId": "gmail:18f3a2b9c0d1e000",
      "from": "Plumber <ana@example.com>",
      "subject": "Mount St plumber quote",
      "date": "2026-08-26T21:05:00.000Z",
      "summary": "First quote, $1,480, not itemised.",
      "isFlagged": false,
      "labels": ["properties/mount st"],
      "systemLabels": [],
      "threadId": "18f3a2b9c0d1e000",
      "threadRole": "child",
      "inInbox": false,             // already archived → its action can only be "archive"
      "decision": {
        "emailAction": "archive",   // DERIVED from the head (page), never chosen by Gabriel
        "isTask": false,
        "flagged": false,           // children are never starred
        "labels": ["properties/mount st"],
        "task": null
      }
    },
    {
      // ── An OUTLOOK head that becomes a NEW task ──
      "id": "AAMkAGI2...",
      "source": "outlook",
      "sourceId": "outlook:AAMkAGI2...",
      "from": "Council <rates@council.gov.au>",
      "subject": "Rates notice due 15 Sep",
      "date": "2026-08-28T22:14:00.000Z",
      "summary": "Council rates $612 due 15 Sep; pay via BPAY.",
      "isFlagged": false,
      // (no labels / systemLabels keys: Outlook email)
      "threadId": "AAQkAGI2...",
      "threadRole": "head",
      "inInbox": true,
      "category": "Important",
      "existingTaskKey": null,
      "suggestedTask": {
        "title": "Huberts: Pay council rates ($612)",   // prefix already applied by step 1
        "notes": "-- notes\n\n-- auto --\nPay $612 by BPAY before 15 Sep.\n28 Aug — rates notice issued\nLatest email: https://outlook.live.com/mail/0/inbox/id/AAMkAGI2...\n[triage] thread=AAQkAGI2... src=outlook",
        "dueDate": "2026-09-15",    // "YYYY-MM-DD" or "" for none
        "link": "https://outlook.live.com/mail/0/inbox/id/AAMkAGI2..."   // deep link to the HEAD
      },
      "decision": {
        "emailAction": "create-task",
        "isTask": true,
        "flagged": true,
        "task": null                // Gabriel edited nothing → suggestedTask is created as-is
      }
    }
  ],

  // ── Existing tasks (Google Tasks / Microsoft To Do) ─────────────────────
  // Step 1 writes the open (and recently completed) tasks it fetched — at least
  // every task referenced by an existingTaskKey. Step 1 writes every field
  // except `decision` (page) and `outcome` (step 3). Values must be the CURRENT
  // backend values — the page diffs against them and records only what changed.
  "existingTasks": [
    {
      "key": "gtasks:MTIz:abc789",   // "<provider>:<listId>:<taskId>" — THE identity
      "provider": "gtasks",          // "gtasks" | "todo" — also decides the tab
      "listId": "MTIz",
      "listName": "My Tasks",
      "url": null,                   // optional display link; may be null (the page then shows plain text)
      "title": "Mount: plumber quote",   // READ-ONLY after creation — never renamed, no `title` in edits
      // The live description, both sections (see the header for the format).
      "notes": "-- notes\nAsk about the water damage too.\n\n-- auto --\n27 Aug — quote requested\nLatest email: https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/18f2...\n[triage] thread=18f3a2b9c0d1e000 src=gmail",
      "status": "needsAction",       // "needsAction" | "completed" — a completed task is read-only everywhere
      "dueDate": "2026-09-05",       // "YYYY-MM-DD" or ""
      "link": "https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/18f2...",   // the message the task currently points at
      "threadId": "18f3a2b9c0d1e000",   // parsed from the [triage] footer

      // Step 2 owns this block. Step 1 may omit it.
      "decision": {
        "complete": false,         // true ⇒ mark the task completed  (mirrors emailAction "complete-task")
        "cancel": false,           // true ⇒ same, plus a "Cancelled DD Mon: …" line (mirrors "cancel-task")
        // null = nothing changed. Otherwise ONLY the keys that differ from the
        // values above; step 3 applies exactly these. There is no `title` key.
        "edits": {
          // Full new description: Gabriel's -- notes section + the -- auto -- block, unchanged.
          "notes": "-- notes\nAsk about the water damage too.\nAnd the gutter.\n\n-- auto --\n27 Aug — quote requested\nLatest email: https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/18f2...\n[triage] thread=18f3a2b9c0d1e000 src=gmail",
          "dueDate": "2026-09-04",
          // Repointed at the newest message of the thread. The page defaults this
          // whenever the head is `newInThread`; step 3 rewrites the "Latest email:"
          // line with it (and, on To Do, linkedResources[0].webUrl).
          "link": "https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/18f3a2b9c0d1e999"
        }
      },

      // Step 3 only, e.g. "updated", "completed", "cancelled", "untouched",
      // "task already completed", "FAILED: …"
      "outcome": "updated"
    }
  ],

  // ── New tasks added by Gabriel on the page ──────────────────────────────
  // Step 1 writes an empty array (or omits it). Step 2 appends. Step 3 creates
  // each one in the backend named by `provider`, which also decides its tab.
  "newTasks": [
    {
      "title": "Renew passport",
      "notes": "-- notes\nExpires Feb 2027 — book appointment.\n\n-- auto --",
      "provider": "todo",         // "gtasks" | "todo" — the tab it was added from
      "dueDate": "",
      "outcome": "created"        // step 3 only
    }
  ]
}

// =============================================================================
//  Step-by-step responsibilities
// =============================================================================
//
//  STEP 1 — pa-email-triage (creates the file; overwrite any previous session)
//    • generatedAt; groups = { gabriel: {…}, "gabriel-arina": {…} }, both pending — exactly
//      those two keys, each { status: "pending-review", reviewedAt: null, processedAt: null }.
//      NO top-level status key.
//    • gmailLabels: every user-created label of the Gabriel & Arina Gmail.
//    • mailboxes: which connectors were fetched.
//    • emails[]: EVERY message of every thread that has at least one inbox
//      message — id, source, sourceId, from, subject, date, summary, isFlagged,
//      threadId, threadRole ("head" = newest, one per thread), inInbox; gmail
//      only: labels = user labels, systemLabels = all other labels minus
//      INBOX/STARRED. HEADS also get category, existingTaskKey | null,
//      suggestedTask | null and newInThread. No decision / outcome.
//      isFlagged: Gmail = message has STARRED; Outlook = flagStatus "flagged".
//    • existingTasks[] from Google Tasks + Microsoft To Do with current values
//      (key, provider, listId, listName, url | null, title, notes, status,
//      dueDate, link, threadId parsed from the [triage] footer) — no decision /
//      outcome. Match a task to a head by that threadId.
//    • newTasks: []
//    • Task notes: read the `-- notes` section, keep it byte-for-byte, and
//      regenerate everything below `-- auto --` (timeline + latest-email link +
//      [triage] footer). New tasks get an empty `-- notes` section and a title
//      that already carries the properties/* prefix.
//
//  STEP 2 — triage-review.html (mutates in place, per tab)
//    • Fills every emails[].decision (incl. decision.labels for gmail and the
//      DERIVED decisions of every child) and existingTasks[].decision, appends
//      newTasks. Only heads are interactive; only the `-- notes` half of a
//      description is editable; a task title is never written.
//    • Confirm & Save on a tab: groups.<tab> = { status: "reviewed", reviewedAt: now,
//      processedAt: null } for THAT TAB ONLY, then writes the whole file.
//      Skip on a tab: same with status "skipped". Reopen (skipped → pending) sets
//      reviewedAt back to null. The other tab is never touched.
//    • Refuses to write if groups.<tab>.status on disk is not what it last saw.
//    • Never writes processedAt or any outcome field.
//    • Assumes a file written by the current step 1 — there is no migration and
//      no backwards compatibility.
//
//  STEP 3 — pa-email-triage-save (mutates in place, per group)
//    • GATE: if groups.gabriel.status or groups["gabriel-arina"].status is "pending-review",
//      stop and change nothing — Gabriel must Confirm or Skip every tab first.
//    • For EACH group whose groups.<g>.status === "reviewed":
//        – emails of that group: perform decision.emailAction (table above).
//          For "create-task" create decision.task ?? suggestedTask in that
//          mailbox's task app (Google Tasks for gmail, To Do for outlook).
//          Then star/flag: decision.flagged !== isFlagged → Gmail STARRED
//          add/remove or Outlook flag_email; every action, archived emails
//          included. Gmail emails: also apply the USER label diff (labels →
//          decision.labels); never touch systemLabels. An email with inInbox
//          false is never moved back to the inbox.
//        – existingTasks of that group: apply decision.edits (only the keys
//          present — notes / dueDate / link; never a title), then
//          decision.complete → completed, decision.cancel → completed plus a
//          "Cancelled DD Mon: …" line in the auto block. A task whose status is
//          already "completed" is left alone.
//        – newTasks of that group: create in the backend named by `provider`.
//        – re-read the live task before writing so a `-- notes` section Gabriel
//          typed since the fetch survives, and always keep the [triage] footer.
//        – stamp `outcome` on every item touched (string; "FAILED: …" on errors).
//        – set groups.<g>.status = "processed" (or "processed-with-errors" if any
//          item failed) and groups.<g>.processedAt = now.
//    • Never touch a "skipped" group (leave its status "skipped") or one that is
//      already "processed" / "processed-with-errors".
//    • Do NOT add a top-level status (or any other session-level status) — the
//      two group statuses are the only ones. Write the whole file back.
// =============================================================================
